    {
      "annotations": {
        "readOnlyHint": true,
      },
      "description": "Read the current pipeline state by run_id. format:'summary' (default) returns the lightweight envelope; format:'full' returns the whole state, bounded to the Claude Code 100,000-char MCP response budget by shedding least-relevant detail first (observable __bounded markers; full grounding re-fetchable via format:'grounding'); format:'grounding' returns the codebase_grounding (+ prd_validation when it fits) blobs format:'full' sheds first; format:'validation' returns prd_validation alone (the blob format:'grounding' sheds when the pair overshoots); format:'action' returns the last action (refreshing a pending verification question) with full spawn_subagents prompts — the recovery path when a start_pipeline/submit_action_result response's __bounded.applied records action.invocations[].prompt: the prompts from that record's next_offset on are omitted stubs, and next_offset is the invocation_offset to read them from. It is paged under the same budget: each page holds whole invocations from invocation_offset (default 0), and __page.next_offset is the offset of the next page, null on the last one. format:'define_handoff_v1' returns validated planning data from completed automatic review or a pending legacy checkpoint. format:'verified_plan_v1' derives and verifies a one-Step plan from that checkpoint. format:'implementation_review_v1' reads the operator-approved plan and its pinned Git comparison for review.",
      "execution": {
        "taskSupport": "forbidden",
